  "post": {
    "caption": "The Hope Diamond hung on a dog. In 1911, Evalyn McLean and her husband bought the Hope Diamond from Pierre Cartier. She wore it everywhere around Washington, even for gardening. At parties, she hid it and challenged her guests to find it. In the 1920s, it also hung from her dog's collar. She hired a former Secret Service man to guard it. Harry Winston bought it from her estate in 1949, and in 1958 he gave it to the Smithsonian, where it is kept. The Hope Diamond weighs 45.52 carats.",
